# Copy to .env and fill in — .env is gitignored and must NEVER be committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Then either export these in your shell before `npm start`, or use a loader
# such as `node --env-file=.env server.js` (Node 20+).

# Required for problem generation. Create the key inside a WORKSPACE at
# https://console.anthropic.com — an organisation-level key is rejected.
# Without this the site still runs; the Analyse box just disables itself.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Only needed if your key is NOT scoped to a workspace.
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=

# Models are chosen per task. Defaults:
#   analyse → claude-sonnet-5   recall + classification
#   trace   → claude-opus-5     the hard one; a wrong trace is worse than none
#   C++     → claude-sonnet-5   short and fully specified by then
# Override one:
# STEPWISE_MODEL_ANALYZE=claude-haiku-4-5
# STEPWISE_MODEL_BUILD=claude-opus-5
# STEPWISE_MODEL_CODE=claude-haiku-4-5
#
# Or override all three at once — useful for a cheap exploratory run:
# STEPWISE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Identical requests are cached on disk and cost nothing to repeat.
# Set to 0 to force every call to hit the API.
# STEPWISE_CACHE=0

# Optional. Defaults to 8765.
# PORT=8765
